# novadeck build-provenance markers — paths that must NEVER reach a shipped root.
#
# One tree-relative path per line (no leading /); blank lines and #-comments ignored.
#
#   <path>            must exist in the base — assemble-rootfs.sh reports it if it does not, which
#                     is how a typo'd path (absent from every tree, so asserted by nobody, forever)
#                     gets caught instead of silently weakening the guard.
#   <path> optional   defensive entry for a marker this builder does not produce. Scrubbed and
#                     asserted exactly the same; only the not-found report is suppressed, so the
#                     report stays worth reading.
#
# We bootstrap from a vendor-built container image (base.digest), so the staged tree starts life
# carrying artifacts of two build systems that are not ours: docker's, and the vendor's CI. This
# file is the single declaration of what those are. images/assemble-rootfs.sh removes every line
# from the staged tree; images/guard-rootfs.sh then asserts every line is gone before an image is
# built from it. Both read THIS file, so a marker can never be scrubbed-but-unasserted (or the
# reverse), and adding one on a base bump is a one-line reviewable diff.
#
# Phase 4c (bootstrap from packages into an empty root, dropping the `base` lock class) deletes
# the need for this file entirely — nothing is inherited, so nothing has to be scrubbed. Until
# then this is the maintenance tax of the docker-export bootstrap, kept explicit and named.

# --- docker ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `systemd-detect-virt` reports a container when these exist, and systemd then SILENTLY skips
# every ConditionVirtualization=!container unit — ~13 of them, systemd-timesyncd being the visible
# casualty (clock stuck at epoch). HW-confirmed 2026-06-25.
.dockerenv
run/.containerenv optional   # podman's; we build with docker, so it is never present here

# --- vendor CI ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Artifacts of the base image's own build pipeline. Functionally inert, but they are someone
# else's build metadata shipping as part of our OS. Found 2026-07-26 by an unowned-file audit of
# the pinned base (31,203 files, 30,012 owned by a package); both were reaching the image.
repos
etc/mash-ci-tracking.job_id
